{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0376","billNumberShort":"H.B. 376","billNumberLong":"HB0376S01","fileNumber":"2026FL1017","shortTitle":"Land Management Funding Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"ALBRECR","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Albrecht, Carl R.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"SANDASD","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Sandall, Scott D.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses funding for watershed restoration and forest health.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>establishes the Utah Forest Restoration Institute (institute) in connection with Utah State University;<hr><ltbullet>provides funding to the institute;<hr><ltbullet>requires the institute to:<hr><ltbullet1>conduct research as provided by state and federal law;<hr><ltbullet1>study how the state can improve forest and watershed health;<hr><ltbullet1>recommend mitigation strategies that reduce the risks and impact of wildfire;<hr><ltbullet1>coordinate with the Watershed Restoration Initiative to fund watershed and forest restoration projects;<hr><ltbullet1>review and respond to, in a timely manner, an emergency request for funding a watershed restoration project in response to a natural disaster; and<hr><ltbullet1>monitor the long-term effectiveness of watershed and forest restoration projects;<hr><ltbullet>requires the Watershed Restoration Initiative to:<hr><ltbullet1>coordinate funding decisions with the institute on partnership watershed restoration projects;<hr><ltbullet1>coordinate the long-term monitoring of a watershed restoration project with the institute;<hr><ltbullet1>collect data required by the institute; <hr><ltbullet1>provide research and learning opportunities for higher education students and faculty associated with the institute; and<hr><ltbullet1>submit an annual report to the institute and two legislative committees; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"","draftingAttorney":"Ryan C. Williams","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"NBCJYJSEJD","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-26 10:56:35.773","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-26 10:56:35.773","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill assigned to staff for fiscal analysis for HB0376","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Analyst","actionDate":"2026-01-26 10:56:40.930","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA1","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill sent to agencies for fiscal input for HB0376","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Agency","actionDate":"2026-01-26 10:56:40.930","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA2","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"House/ received bill from Legislative Research","owner":"Clerk of the House","actionDate":"2026-01-26 12:51:59.000","actionClass":"H","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"HRECLRGC","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ fiscal note sent to sponsor for HB0376","owner":"Version Sponsor","actionDate":"2026-01-27 10:47:38.681","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA3","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"House/ 1st reading (Introduced)","owner":"House Rules Committee","actionDate":"2026-01-27 11:20:15.000","actionClass":"H","voteID":"","voiceVote":"